                <pb facs="0857" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Trueblood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-03T16:00:00-04:32">July 3, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>71. The Bolivian Minister in Asuncion was given definite instructions on
                    Wednesday night to leave at once if Paraguayan reply was <pb facs="0858" n="744"
                        xml:id="pg744"/> unsatisfactory and the reply has been so considered here.
                    The Bolivian Foreign Minister stated last night that the Minister would have to
                    leave today if it were on foot but the Foreign Office has at this date received
                    no advices of his departure nor has the Paraguayan Minister here received
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trueblood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
